/// Semantic color tone for a leverage input section's value + unit.
/// 
/// Rust emits **intent only** — the dual long side is `Up`, the dual short side
/// is `Down`, every other scenario is `Neutral`. Native maps the tone to a
/// themed color (the user's rise/fall color preference + Classic/Modern theme +
/// dark mode), which is platform state Rust cannot resolve. **Never emit a
/// literal color from Rust** — that would ignore the user's preference and break
/// dark mode. Mirrors V1 `ContractDualItemFragment`'s side-tinted leverage,
/// moved Rust-side so Native renders without branching on `pos_side`.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
pub enum LeverageColorTone {
    /// Long / up side → native maps to the "rise" color.
    Up,
    /// Short / down side → native maps to the "fall" color.
    Down,
    /// No tint → native keeps the default neutral color.
    Neutral,
}

