/// Per-scenario page chrome, carried in each child interactor state and copied
/// into `AdjustLeverPageVo` by the scenario mapper.
/// 
/// `apply_to` lives on the mapper side (facade) to avoid a `common -> facade`
/// dependency cycle; the mapper just reads these three fields.
/// 
/// `uniffi::Record` because it is a field of the `#[interactor::state]` child
/// states (e.g. `AdjustLeverAccountRiskState`), which are lifted across the FFI
/// boundary -- every state field must be uniffi-representable. All three fields
/// are `DisplayString` (already a uniffi type), so this is zero-cost modeling.
